[{:db/id "q-340497/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "c80b7c79-cc29-58c6-b60f-df2b2e3e3a06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340497/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "576f6ca5-cb08-55f1-86bc-3bdcb32c3baf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340497/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-340497/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340497" :question/id #uuid "4e0a8708-378d-5d66-80bc-b6c370d775c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-340497" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=-4{e}^{2-x}$ at the point where $x=2-ln⁡(3).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=-4{e}^{u},\\,u=2-x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-4{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-4{e}^{u}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4{e}^{u} \\\\  & =4{e}^{2-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=2-ln⁡(3)$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=2-ln⁡(3)} & =4{e}^{2-(2-ln⁡(3))} \\\\  & =4{e}^{ln⁡(3)} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340497/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a83f86ab-a008-5487-b118-f1495a0fe4d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340497"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48658/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "31cc3c23-fa04-52c6-9c9d-b75b2cb87b6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48658/selection/de65f68b9ebe8220ad685ae8fd317e4e85f600952fac99fcca3864668321a3a0" :answer/id #uuid "5031a155-b2b6-5774-9ca0-d8af2045f9d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48658/selection/4134ad333d71889488b18c67e0381aaf1d62d5f4f83f90d0bd77e89f25c47bf0" :answer/id #uuid "183bb6a2-7fe6-5490-8bc8-692844a859df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48658/selection/2372eaf10d3e3c6104c5a2d85d5b9909ce1a56c36600fa4c17241dbcaf0762b2" :answer/id #uuid "048375af-c9c3-596e-b5bf-59742e761c6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48658/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "44e2ce75-e3fb-5415-8a97-086854a9078c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48658/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90d1051a-b535-51a2-8e05-e70fbe39380c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48658/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer-field/choices ["q-48658/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-48658/selection/de65f68b9ebe8220ad685ae8fd317e4e85f600952fac99fcca3864668321a3a0" "q-48658/selection/4134ad333d71889488b18c67e0381aaf1d62d5f4f83f90d0bd77e89f25c47bf0" "q-48658/selection/2372eaf10d3e3c6104c5a2d85d5b9909ce1a56c36600fa4c17241dbcaf0762b2" "q-48658/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48658" :question/id #uuid "fca352cd-c420-5e34-a17c-b3f00c5f450b" :question/math-academy-id "q-48658" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=-3{e}^{5-x}$ at the point where $x=5-ln⁡(2).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=-3{e}^{u},\\,u=5-x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-3{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{u}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =3{e}^{u} \\\\  & =3{e}^{5-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=5-ln⁡(2)$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=5-ln⁡(2)} & =3{e}^{5-(5-ln⁡(2))} \\\\  & =3{e}^{ln⁡(2)} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48658/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a83f86ab-a008-5487-b118-f1495a0fe4d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48658"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48657/selection/6a6fbcd05f9c33ee352d1cf4f0ddb6a099ab759b7fe79a80c5f32142ae09187d" :answer/id #uuid "a4f77739-e4e6-5d69-8262-7b2808f0221a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=20ex" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48657/selection/6bb216da246ba00193b4009f4331d8344723918882a5750dd35bb76969bba14e" :answer/id #uuid "78db1e6f-690b-54a4-90f1-8f1df3a0ed76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=5ex" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48657/selection/137341153da156996a628dbe55e8a8a75d05b28c8bb13bfde7b8619a992a9b4d" :answer/id #uuid "cda33701-cda1-570e-b85d-e13aa2e3d2f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4ex" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48657/selection/9c3647463478c10e3608e6f66ead64cc4dad00f0725c3ddd129f16f43117a4a4" :answer/id #uuid "1a0fffd4-74bc-58d7-b483-57ebfa44de89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=20ex\\cdot ln⁡(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48657/selection/13fd96360fa8e3bbde5958d920f35faa5134ac3ab58448b7ab980e387e21e934" :answer/id #uuid "ca670f03-1065-5401-8b8c-09fc7569ee08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=ex" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48657/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "414233af-99f2-5e00-bea1-764d640b05c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48657/selection/6a6fbcd05f9c33ee352d1cf4f0ddb6a099ab759b7fe79a80c5f32142ae09187d" :answer-field/choices ["q-48657/selection/6a6fbcd05f9c33ee352d1cf4f0ddb6a099ab759b7fe79a80c5f32142ae09187d" "q-48657/selection/6bb216da246ba00193b4009f4331d8344723918882a5750dd35bb76969bba14e" "q-48657/selection/137341153da156996a628dbe55e8a8a75d05b28c8bb13bfde7b8619a992a9b4d" "q-48657/selection/9c3647463478c10e3608e6f66ead64cc4dad00f0725c3ddd129f16f43117a4a4" "q-48657/selection/13fd96360fa8e3bbde5958d920f35faa5134ac3ab58448b7ab980e387e21e934"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48657" :question/id #uuid "5aebbdf2-595a-524c-bde1-ffc1725d278e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48657" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=5{e}^{4x}$ at the point where $x=\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=5{e}^{u},\\,u=4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=5{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =5{e}^{u}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =20{e}^{u} \\\\  & =20{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=\\frac{1}{4}$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=1/4} & ={(20{e}^{4x})|}_{x=1/4} \\\\  & =20{e}^{4(1/4)} \\\\  & =20e\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, the $y$-value of the point on the curve where $x={x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={(5{e}^{4x})|}_{x=1/4} \\\\  & =5{e}^{4(1/4)} \\\\  & =5e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =m(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-5e & =20e(x-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ y-5e & =20ex-5e \\\\ y & =20ex\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48657/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a83f86ab-a008-5487-b118-f1495a0fe4d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48657"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48007/selection/c1836a4844ecd27514973c4b2aa09c255b82194f547cc206a19903aeefb7f316" :answer/id #uuid "29e92247-03ea-5dfa-a7f9-1a600fdc8e58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8{e}^{4x-1}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48007/selection/be611dbfe4b660ca1ca3dac0298e1d25da48cac7dff7ad91d6a89ae74d61aab3" :answer/id #uuid "8abcae28-d559-5e52-8243-4d2cd9c4f8e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8{e}^{4x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48007/selection/a848545aa9d0054a0eccaa391e020d5820743437cb03062738be20ccac6bf547" :answer/id #uuid "06d36fb4-8b11-5be3-9aba-f49d2c4831b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{4x-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48007/selection/e32db641497326c42d7311f7a54443ca28ddb41b387277b91992bad6e779ecff" :answer/id #uuid "a273d5be-0c27-5579-9562-30cb2c1dee76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{e}^{4x-1}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48007/selection/5288ebf743d1707dd8e6933d096cbb612cd76589a53cfdd9e065c520ac719cb7" :answer/id #uuid "2b930837-dfd6-5922-bb79-c8480fc9eabb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8{e}^{4x-2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48007/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd533477-a78f-58dd-8434-35e2d2b44216" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48007/selection/be611dbfe4b660ca1ca3dac0298e1d25da48cac7dff7ad91d6a89ae74d61aab3" :answer-field/choices ["q-48007/selection/c1836a4844ecd27514973c4b2aa09c255b82194f547cc206a19903aeefb7f316" "q-48007/selection/be611dbfe4b660ca1ca3dac0298e1d25da48cac7dff7ad91d6a89ae74d61aab3" "q-48007/selection/a848545aa9d0054a0eccaa391e020d5820743437cb03062738be20ccac6bf547" "q-48007/selection/e32db641497326c42d7311f7a54443ca28ddb41b387277b91992bad6e779ecff" "q-48007/selection/5288ebf743d1707dd8e6933d096cbb612cd76589a53cfdd9e065c520ac719cb7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48007" :question/id #uuid "6f1bd2ce-06f4-50a6-ab3a-1e29b9357ffa" :question/math-academy-id "q-48007" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=-2{e}^{4x-1}+3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=-2{e}^{u}+3,\\,u=4x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=-2{e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-2{e}^{u}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-8{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-8{e}^{4x-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48007/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a83f86ab-a008-5487-b118-f1495a0fe4d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48007"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340496/field-1/3147b496c0da2b853205f96bd9921b81381ee7af74f662d69266f2afda4eac14" :answer/id #uuid "3c35c0b8-2411-5144-9703-7454a558ca0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8-3e^{-3x+5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340496/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "30cab8fe-923d-536c-9351-d3098362f816" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340496/field-1/3147b496c0da2b853205f96bd9921b81381ee7af74f662d69266f2afda4eac14" :answer-field/choices ["q-340496/field-1/3147b496c0da2b853205f96bd9921b81381ee7af74f662d69266f2afda4eac14"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340496" :question/id #uuid "404995e1-01a1-5fec-bf0c-884d2a9c9780" :question/math-academy-id "q-340496" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ if $f(x)=8x+{e}^{-3x+5}.$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y={e}^{-3x+5}$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={e}^{u},\\,u=-3x+5.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-3.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-3{e}^{u} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-3x+5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the sum rule of differentiation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8x+{e}^{-3x+5}) \\\\  & =8-3{e}^{-3x+5} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{-3x+5}+8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340496/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a83f86ab-a008-5487-b118-f1495a0fe4d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340496"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107437/selection/9145fab0e71c83cf1dbfcfbde27dea916e69c76cdef54b632e842a98e914b828" :answer/id #uuid "9a716dc8-cf23-509f-a359-d535efbeb0a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{x}^{4}{e}^{{x}^{5}+1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107437/selection/7f