}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={e}^{u},\\,u=8-2{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-6{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (-6{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-6{x}^{2}{e}^{8-2{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48629/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "107eaf98-be8c-5fb1-ac4c-948b1e00df0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48629"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107452/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "d3bafd23-09da-5dca-ac5d-8c28e0b7c2ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107452/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "1263fa13-a3af-5c6b-9cea-4c1ddcd1e641" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107452/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "5a2e30a1-b7c9-5df3-bd5a-b9af763f1b6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107452/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "e41e2e37-bc1d-5137-8df8-dc6c0b4ae3ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107452/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "88e48b5c-02d0-5789-b3a7-1c1592421bd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107452/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "03a1c15d-7f6a-599c-b0e5-eb1949f001f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107452/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-107452/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" "q-107452/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-107452/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-107452/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" "q-107452/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107452" :question/id #uuid "fe2b30b6-b282-5eeb-91bd-46c1f612de4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107452" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y={e}^{{x}^{3}-4x}$ at the point where $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={e}^{u},\\,u={x}^{3}-4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-4) \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}-4){e}^{{x}^{3}-4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=2$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(3{x}^{2}-4){e}^{{x}^{3}-4x}\\,|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =(3(2)^{2}-4){e}^{{2}^{3}-4(2)} \\\\  & =8\\cdot {e}^{0} \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107452/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "107eaf98-be8c-5fb1-ac4c-948b1e00df0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107452"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340949/field-1/d0e3dc47c72215bc78fa0edcb4aae873c86949930c8e1a7fab33a96f4d5bad31" :answer/id #uuid "4ab3d0c1-7bc1-5747-9f13-f61027a541e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12e^4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340949/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a875bf6-2743-5e2e-9cfd-a8adca47b189" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340949/field-1/d0e3dc47c72215bc78fa0edcb4aae873c86949930c8e1a7fab33a96f4d5bad31" :answer-field/choices ["q-340949/field-1/d0e3dc47c72215bc78fa0edcb4aae873c86949930c8e1a7fab33a96f4d5bad31"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340949" :question/id #uuid "6cca5501-68ec-5237-a389-4b4fb8c8de8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340949" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y={e}^{4{x}^{3}}$ at the point where $x=1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={e}^{u},\\,u=4{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={e}^{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=12{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\cdot (12{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =12{x}^{2}{e}^{u} \\\\  & =12{x}^{2}{e}^{4{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=1$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(12{x}^{2}{e}^{4{x}^{3}})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =12(1)^{2}{e}^{4(1)^{3}} \\\\  & =12{e}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340949/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "107eaf98-be8c-5fb1-ac4c-948b1e00df0a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340949"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-340969/field-1/dbfc441f3c2da50ba904b59f03032049e5788bc0b09744af3b4cc34342aa7ab5" :answer/id #uuid "8c0520ab-7c0b-5598-a9ee-c2ccf4cecb48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\ln(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340969/field-1/8613c27eb83ea4d0384d811aaab62605a9c14614206dd3d9a768937db449092c" :answer/id #uuid "7fd28a88-626e-53a7-bde1-3395cec5d442" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\ln(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-340969/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8fb51ef2-f2c1-51af-8e53-40e912184d71" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-340969/field-1/dbfc441f3c2da50ba904b59f03032049e5788bc0b09744af3b4cc34342aa7ab5" :answer-field/choices ["q-340969/field-1/dbfc441f3c2da50ba904b59f03032049e5788bc0b09744af3b4cc34342aa7ab5" "q-340969/field-1/8613c27eb83ea4d0384d811aaab62605a9c14614206dd3d9a768937db449092c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-340969" :question/id #uuid "451d7bb8-62d7-59f7-8d83-cd6031533c99" :question/math-academy-id "q-340969" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y={5}^{x-{x}^{3}}$ at the point where $x=1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={5}^{u},\\,u=x-{x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={5}^{u}ln⁡(5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1-3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={5}^{u}ln⁡(5)\\cdot (1-3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =(1-3{x}^{2}){5}^{x-{x}^{3}}ln⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=1$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={((1-3{x}^{2}){5}^{x-{x}^{3}}ln⁡(5))|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =(1-3(1)^{2}){5}^{1-(1)^{3}}ln⁡(5) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {5}^{0}ln⁡(5) \\\\  & =-2ln⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-340969/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f4bfd24-dafd-57b3-940a-154a6e0acf3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-340969"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-312462/field-1/0e30edc57e5035f9d92350f0bb298f17121831317421a32c506f522f61f4e400" :answer/id #uuid "d8f8895d-c35f-5010-9339-3690d53403f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x^2\\ln(5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-312462/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "497e3e33-d3a1-5812-8d19-45cd27ffa318" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-312462/field-1/0e30edc57e5035f9d92350f0bb298f17121831317421a32c506f522f61f4e400" :answer-field/choices ["q-312462/field-1/0e30edc57e5035f9d92350f0bb298f17121831317421a32c506f522f61f4e400"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-312462" :question/id #uuid "31adc78d-486d-58f1-977f-a0fc1dc4dc68" :question/math-academy-id "q-312462" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={5}^{{x}^{3}+1},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\,{5}^{{x}^{3}+1}$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={5}^{u},\\,u={x}^{3}+1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={5}^{u}ln⁡(5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={5}^{u}ln⁡(5)\\cdot (3{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{u} \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}ln⁡(5)\\cdot {5}^{{x}^{3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-312462/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f4bfd24-dafd-57b3-940a-154a6e0acf3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-312462"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107461/selection/17345889ed05e24070720944579bc71313f2acd617d49ee200a08b00e2128987" :answer/id #uuid "d90fd5a9-b1f3-5548-a666-a4f8f072741a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\cdot {6}^{1-4x}ln⁡6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107461/selection/563dab3b1368004d7d77d46939219b2c3887e6564d7d08d3ed57b09f43ab5707" :answer/id #uuid "065a7ac1-8621-5e79-a54e-43bc66fc881c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24\\cdot {6}^{1-4x}ln⁡6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107461/selection/7141356ef94e49c4431ce0c18afd027fa8e7e7d6c9d1f2e02ffcbde21939a5f9" :answer/id #uuid "062d0e45-6cea-5d76-9ca2-0b69c9b120a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\cdot {6}^{1-4x}ln⁡6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107461/selection/fc44855d15c8764dd6a9283a66bbef212b0188c75e102169e05112962d253524" :answer/id #uuid "7c10ff58-e030-5aa7-b5d7-65d611a95b84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\cdot {6}^{1-4x}ln⁡6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107461/selection/c50d746c5942e3255181f9d1c3cfb9cd6b1dbc690a84fbe22bce037ffaa7712c" :answer/id #uuid "96f76ef0-d045-5c1d-a052-5e3bcb6318db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\cdot {6}^{1-4x}ln⁡6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107461/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5367b2e7-5401-5181-91a9-d1b63476d191" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107461/selection/17345889ed05e24070720944579bc71313f2acd617d49ee200a08b00e2128987" :answer-field/choices ["q-107461/selection/17345889ed05e24070720944579bc71313f2acd617d49ee200a08b00e2128987" "q-107461/selection/563dab3b1368004d7d77d46939219b2c3887e6564d7d08d3ed57b09f43ab5707" "q-107461/selection/7141356ef94e49c4431ce0c18afd027fa8e7e7d6c9d1f2e02ffcbde21939a5f9" "q-107461/selection/fc44855d15c8764dd6a9283a66bbef212b0188c75e102169e05112962d253524" "q-107461/selection/c50d746c5942e3255181f9d1c3cfb9cd6b1dbc690a84fbe22bce037ffaa7712c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107461" :question/id #uuid "1d990be1-9c91-5fc6-a2bf-7e557cb860c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-107461" :question/is-example false :question/problem "If $f(x)={6}^{1-4x},$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={6}^{u},\\,u=1-4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}={6}^{u}ln⁡6,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={6}^{u}ln⁡6\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot {6}^{u}ln⁡6 \\\\  & =-4\\cdot {6}^{1-4x}ln⁡6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107461/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f4bfd24-dafd-57b3-940a-154a6e0acf3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107461"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-48659/selection/72839c9ed45c755d2427fbcd9f49c2796b662269a36433e99ba81225fb4cb407" :answer/id #uuid "9b123f53-94a3-59a5-b031-69722960b0d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28ln⁡(4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48659/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5bf0c7e6-c687-5f09-ad9d-3e2b6b77e8fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48659/selection/f8fa74033dec4e27ab77f5feb6c96e33b41d63848e2f22ed860b16470a2aa0fb" :answer/id #uuid "a5cbb9a1-5e36-5d68-8846-b1777adfadd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4ln⁡(4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48659/selection/3d004effad86642aea58e209ada1aa9d532cc466e176c1600f77eb0744fefaa2" :answer/id #uuid "39b9da26-383a-5cf6-bb9f-4549c5132d3f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7ln⁡(4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48659/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "6f5dd949-9579-5e18-9ae4-9936263f843e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48659/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8e28b7c-8fe8-53fe-8b78-f4b3064f4084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48659/selection/72839c9ed45c755d2427fbcd9f49c2796b662269a36433e99ba81225fb4cb407" :answer-field/choices ["q-48659/selection/72839c9ed45c755d2427fbcd9f49c2796b662269a36433e99ba81225fb4cb407" "q-48659/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-48659/selection/f8fa74033dec4e27ab77f5feb6c96e33b41d63848e2f22ed860b16470a2aa0fb" "q-48659/selection/3d004effad86642aea58e209ada1aa9d532cc466e176c1600f77eb0744fefaa2" "q-48659/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48659" :question/id #uuid "d0869377-9313-5d2b-ad1e-f39197afff7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48659" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y={4}^{7x}$ at the point where $x=\\frac{1}{7}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={4}^{u},\\,u=7x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}={4}^{u}ln⁡4,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=7.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={4}^{u}ln⁡4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =7ln⁡4\\cdot {4}^{u} \\\\  & =7ln⁡4\\cdot {4}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the slope of the tangent to the curve at $x=\\frac{1}{7}$, we have to evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{x=1/7} & =7ln⁡(4)\\cdot {4}^{7(1/7)} \\\\  & =7ln⁡(4)\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =28ln⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point where $x=\\frac{1}{7}$ is $28ln⁡(4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-48659/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f4bfd24-dafd-57b3-940a-154a6e0acf3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48659"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107459/selection/95ec25013e312a43fa813ce815e87a369f03505849be45a98f936fe632a777e1" :answer/id #uuid "0b2a06f1-2b56-58b0-a354-adc5cc46e278" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2x\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{2}-1}ln⁡4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107459/selection/2f7498bf336845826f86176d9eaab094ab4ee07a6fb0e0a938491725498530e0" :answer/id #uuid "86da781b-67b7-548a-930d-450588bd2b39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6x\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{2}-1}ln⁡4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107459/selection/2456d3ec2bea0f43254bf010f394f83285347b4ff3df4daaac32d99b0fca0760" :answer/id #uuid "e582eaeb-e77c-5832-9f9c-e4d10da8abf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6x\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{2}-1}ln⁡4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107459/selection/16a5084002752578b37d22ad831989bdd8f80caca24c19d045e2850ad238af14" :answer/id #uuid "e16268fd-f2f6-5590-936e-367c8df7402f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{2}-1}ln⁡4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107459/selection/1b21d627fde614e7697f1097e534b74a95656ea71813e9754e868fe4a26ab70d" :answer/id #uuid "8b838d5d-7a9a-5312-b497-09f1d51087c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{2}-1}ln⁡4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107459/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "060f5355-bd73-5340-8a80-a4c7f0cda5f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107459/selection/2f7498bf336845826f86176d9eaab094ab4ee07a6fb0e0a938491725498530e0" :answer-field/choices ["q-107459/selection/95ec25013e312a43fa813ce815e87a369f03505849be45a98f936fe632a777e1" "q-107459/selection/2f7498bf336845826f86176d9eaab094ab4ee07a6fb0e0a938491725498530e0" "q-107459/selection/2456d3ec2bea0f43254bf010f394f83285347b4ff3df4daaac32d99b0fca0760" "q-107459/selection/16a5084002752578b37d22ad831989bdd8f80caca24c19d045e2850ad238af14" "q-107459/selection/1b21d627fde614e7697f1097e534b74a95656ea71813e9754e868fe4a26ab70d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107459" :question/id #uuid "f148f6ee-4961-587a-83e8-75698f3f5d2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-107459" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Given that $y=3\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{2}-1},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=3\\cdot {4}^{u},\\,u={x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=3\\cdot {4}^{u}ln⁡4,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3\\cdot {4}^{u}ln⁡4\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =6x\\cdot {4}^{{x}^{2}-1}ln⁡4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107459/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f4bfd24-dafd-57b3-940a-154a6e0acf3d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107459"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
